RMDIR(2)                       P32W Unix                        RMDIR(2)

NAME
       rmdir - remove a directory

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       int rmdir(const char *path);

DESCRIPTION
       rmdir removes the directory path, which must be empty: it
       may hold only . and .. . Its parent must be writable, and if
       the parent has the sticky bit set the caller must own the
       directory or be the super-user.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success; -1 on an error, with errno set.

ERRORS
       ENOENT  The directory does not exist, or a directory in
               path does not exist.
       ENOTDIR path, or a component of its prefix, is not a
               directory.
       ENOTEMPTY
               The directory holds entries besides . and .. .
       EACCES  Search permission is denied on a directory in the
               path, or the parent is not writable (or is sticky
               and not the caller's).
       EINVAL  The last component of path is . or ..
       EFAULT  path is a bad address.
       ENAMETOOLONG
               path is 256 characters or more, or a component is
               longer than 28.

SEE ALSO
       mkdir(2), unlink(2), rmdir(1)

BUGS
       rmdir does not check whether the directory is some
       process's current directory or has a filesystem mounted on
       it (the empty directory underneath is removed).
